`#!/bin/bash` – Specifies Bash as the interpreter for executing the shell script.
`echo` – Prints messages or results on the terminal.
`read` – Accepts input from the user and saves it in a variable.
`${str:start:len}` – Extracts a substring using the starting index and length.
`${#str}` – Returns the total length of a string.
`#include <stdio.h>` – Includes the standard library for input and output operations in C.
`#include <string.h>` – Provides string-handling functions such as `strlen()`.
`char` – Defines a character variable or an array of characters.
`int` – Defines variables used to store integer values.
`printf()` – Prints data and messages in a C program.
`scanf()` – Reads user input in a C program.
`for` – Executes a set of statements repeatedly while the condition is true.
`strlen()` – Finds the number of characters in a string, excluding `'\0'`.
`'\0'` – Null character indicating the end of a C string.
`return 0` – Indicates successful program execution.
`gcc` – GNU compiler used to compile C programs.
`chmod +x` – Assigns executable permission to a shell script.
`time` – Calculates the time required to execute a command or program.
`real` – Shows the actual elapsed time of execution.
`user` – Shows the CPU time used by the program in user mode.
`sys` – Shows the CPU time consumed by the operating system on behalf of the program.
